  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the maximum probability of each lottery and prefers the one with the higher maximum probability. In this case, Lottery B has a maximum probability of 100%, which is higher than Lottery A’s 66%, so the reason would select B. The individual also identifies the 100% probability of winning in B (i.e., the maximum probability) as decisive. Although the individual frames it in terms of 'guaranteed win' rather than explicitly referencing 'maximum probability,' the underlying information used (100% vs. less than 100%) and the resulting preference align closely with the logic of the decision reason. The justification, while phrased in natural language, reflects attention to the same core attribute—the highest probability event. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used reasoning consistent with the specified decision rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
